# Notes Documentation Rule

When the user says **"apply the notes_doc rule"** (or similar, e.g. "apply notes_doc.mdc to Files/python.md"), perform the documentation workflow below.

## Workflow Steps

1. **Read** `bin/raw.md` for the raw content.
2. **Read** `bin/old.md` for the accordion template (match its section order, checkbox style, and spacing).
3. **Read** `bin/lab_sample.md` for the Lab section template (Overview, Task headings, `- [ ]` steps).
4. **Analyze** the raw content and map it to the accordion structure:
   - Introduction (plain heading — **not** a child accordion)
   - Detailed Explanation (plain heading — **not** a child accordion; use `- [x]` checkboxes and sub-items)
   - Lab (**child accordion**; step-by-step process as in `bin/lab_sample.md`; see Lab rules below)
   - Terminal Commands (**child accordion**; fenced `bash` blocks with explanations)
   - Code (**child accordion**; fenced code blocks with explanations)
   - Questions and Answers (**child accordion**; 10–20 Q&A; each answer uses nested `<details><summary>Answer</summary>`; see child-accordion and bullet rules below)
   - Summary (plain heading — **not** a child accordion)
   - References (plain heading — **not** a child accordion)
5. **Generate** 10–20 revision Q&A from the content to aid study.
6. **Append** (do not overwrite) the formatted accordion to the **file the user named** when applying this rule. If they did not name a target file, ask which file to append to before writing.

## Format Requirements

- Use HTML `<details>` and `<summary>` for accordion-style sections as in `bin/old.md` and `bin/sample.md`.
- **Accordion spacing:** For every `<details>` block, put **one blank line** after the closing `</summary>` tag and **one blank line** before `</details>`, so the inner content is visually separated from the tags. This applies to **topic** accordions (e.g. `<summary>Topic Title</summary>`), **child** accordions (`Lab`, `Terminal Commands`, `Code`, `Questions and Answers`), and **answer** accordions (`<summary>Answer</summary>`).
- Title for the accordion comes from the first `#` heading in `bin/raw.md`.
- First reference in References must be the source page link (pasted at the top of `bin/raw.md`).
- Every other link from the raw notes should also be added under References after that first link.
- **Child accordions:** Opening a topic must **not** stretch the page with Lab, Terminal Commands, Code, or Q&A. Those four stay in their own closed inner `<details>` blocks. Leave **Introduction**, **Detailed Explanation**, **Summary**, and **References** as normal `##` headings (never wrap those four in child accordions). After Detailed Explanation, emit the four children in this order, then Summary and References. Match `bin/old.md`, `bin/sample.md`, and `bin/lab_sample.md`:

````markdown
<details>
  <summary>Lab</summary>

## Lab

### **Overview**

- [ ] Goal of the walkthrough.

</details>

<details>
  <summary>Terminal Commands</summary>

## Terminal Commands

```bash
# example
```

</details>

<details>
  <summary>Code</summary>

## Code

```text
# example
```

</details>

<details>
  <summary>Questions and Answers</summary>

## Questions and Answers

### Question 1: Example question?

<details>
<summary>Answer</summary>

- [x] Example answer.

</details>

</details>
````

- Each Q&A uses nested `<details><summary>Answer</summary>` **inside the Questions and Answers child accordion**, with blank lines after `</summary>` and before `</details>` as in **Accordion spacing** above.
- **Answer formatting:** Inside `<details><summary>Answer</summary>`, use **checked task-list lines** (`- [x] …`) for every answer line—whether there is **one** fact or **many**. Do **not** use plain `- ` without `[x]` in Q&A answers. For multiple items, put **one `- [x]` line per item**, not one long comma-separated sentence.
- **Lab:** Place the **Lab** child accordion immediately after Detailed Explanation (do not leave `## Lab` in the topic body outside that child). If the raw transcript includes a lab, hands-on project, or console/CLI walkthrough, generate a step-by-step process matching `bin/lab_sample.md` (use `###` under `## Lab` so tasks stay inside this section):
  - Start with `### **Overview**` using `- [ ]` lines that state the goal and what you will do.
  - Then numbered tasks as `### **Task N: Title**` with `- [ ]` steps (unchecked, so the reader can tick them while doing the lab).
  - Nest sub-steps under a task; put console clicks, names, regions, and exact values on their own `- [ ]` lines.
  - Include fenced `bash` / `json` / other code in the task where it is used; wrap long policy/config JSON in `<details>` as in `bin/lab_sample.md`.
  - End the last task with a short success line when the lab has a clear completion point.
  - If there is **no** lab or project in `bin/raw.md`, still include `## Lab` with a brief placeholder, same pattern as Terminal Commands / Code when empty, e.g. `No labs in this topic; the content is conceptual only.`

## Content Guidelines

- Put **Lab**, **Terminal Commands**, **Code**, and **Questions and Answers** each in its own **child** accordion. Do not leave those headings or their bodies in the topic body outside the matching child.
- For **Questions and Answers**, always format the answer body with **`- [x]`** lines inside `<details>`, not bare paragraphs or plain `-` bullets.
- One topic per accordion.
- Preserve all explanations, lab steps, terminal commands, and code from the raw content.
- Use checkboxes (`- [x]`) for breakdown items in Detailed Explanation.
- Use unchecked checkboxes (`- [ ]`) for Lab walkthrough steps (as in `bin/lab_sample.md`); do not use `- [x]` in Lab.
- Include sub-items where appropriate.
- If Terminal Commands, Code, or Lab has no content, still emit the **child accordion** with the heading and a brief placeholder (do not omit the Lab child).

## File Paths

| Purpose                        | Path                                   |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
| Input (raw paste)              | `bin/raw.md`                           |
| Accordion template             | `bin/old.md`                           |
| Compact child-accordion sample | `bin/sample.md`                        |
| Lab template                   | `bin/lab_sample.md`                    |
| Output (append target)         | The file named when applying this rule |
